# The marketing site is a static export. It has no server of its own, no
# session, and no account system: `AuthScreen` is a waitlist form and says so.
#
# This file used to list AUTH_SECRET and three sets of OAuth credentials for
# Auth.js. Nothing read them. The provider file that did was deleted alongside
# this change because it had no call site, would not compile without a
# dependency the site does not install, and could only have re-created the
# sign-in that was deliberately removed for promising an account that does not
# exist. See the comment at the top of components/AuthScreen.tsx.
#
# The one server-side thing the site talks to is the waitlist, which
# lib/waitlist.ts POSTs to /api/waitlist. That endpoint is a managed function
# deployed by the hosting platform, not built from this package, so it takes
# its configuration there rather than here.

# The origin the site is served from. Used to build absolute canonical,
# OpenGraph and sitemap URLs at build time. Falls back to the production
# origin, so a normal build needs nothing set.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://antifailure.dev
